{"task_id": "HumanEval/7", "solution": "```toml\n[project]\nname = \"stringfilter\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A reusable library and tools to filter lists of strings by substring.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\ndependencies = [\n    # No heavy external dependencies by default\n]\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nlicense = { file = \"LICENSE\" }\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\nhttp = [\"Flask>=2.0.0\"]\n\n[project.scripts]\nstringfilter = \"stringfilter.cli_adapter:main\" # Entry point for CLI\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core>=1.0.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"stringfilter\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A reusable library and tools to filter lists of strings by substring.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\npackages = [{ include = \"stringfilter\", from = \"src\" }]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.9\"\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^7.0\"\npytest-cov = \"^4.0\"\nflask = { version = \">=2.0.0\", optional = true } # Flask explicitly listed as optional here for poetry config\n\n[tool.poetry.extras]\nhttp = [\"flask\"]\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nstringfilter = \"stringfilter.cli_adapter:main\"\n```\n\n```markdown\n# StringFilter Library\n\nA Python library and command-line tool for filtering lists of strings by a substring.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Library Function**: `filter_by_substring(items, substring)`\n- **CLI Tool**: `stringfilter filter`\n- **HTTP API**: `POST /filter` (optional Flask dependency)\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install stringfilter\n# For HTTP API:\npip install \"stringfilter[http]\"\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library\n\n```python\nfrom stringfilter import filter_by_substring\n\nitems = ['apple', 'banana', 'cherry', 'date']\nfiltered = filter_by_substring(items, 'an')\nprint(filtered) # Output: ['banana']\n```\n\n### CLI\n\n```bash\n# Filter from a file\necho '[\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]' > input.json\nstringfilter filter --substring \"an\" --input-file input.json\n\n# Filter from stdin (newline-separated)\necho -e \"apple\\nbanana\\ncherry\" | stringfilter filter --substring \"an\"\n\n# Case-insensitive\nstringfilter filter --substring \"A\" --case-insensitive --input-file input.json\n\n# Persist input to a file\necho '[\"one\", \"two\"]' | stringfilter filter --substring \"o\" --persist \"/tmp/audit.json\"\n```\n\n### HTTP API (optional)\n\nRun the Flask app:\n```bash\nexport FLASK_APP=src/stringfilter/api_adapter.py\nflask run\n```\n\nThen make a POST request:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\n  \"items\": [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"],\n  \"substring\": \"an\",\n  \"config\": {\n    \"case_sensitive\": false\n  }\n}' http://127.0.0.1:5000/filter\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"result\": [\"banana\"]\n}\n```\n```\n\n```\nMIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2023 Your Name\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringfilter/__init__.py\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom .models import FilterConfig\nfrom .dto import FilterRequest, FilterResponse\nfrom .filter_service import FilterService\nfrom .filter_controller import FilterController\nfrom .utils import Validator\nfrom .exceptions import FilterError\n\ndef filter_by_substring(strings: List[str], substring: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filter an input list of strings only for ones that contain given substring.\n    >>> filter_by_substring([], 'a')\n    []\n    >>> filter_by_substring(['abc', 'bacd', 'cde', 'array'], 'a')\n    ['abc', 'bacd', 'array']\n    \"\"\"\n    cfg = FilterConfig()\n    service = FilterService(cfg)\n    controller = FilterController(service, Validator())\n    req = FilterRequest(strings, substring, cfg)\n    resp = controller.handle_filter(req)\n    return resp.result\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringfilter/models.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass FilterConfig:\n    \"\"\"Configuration for filtering behavior and limits.\"\"\"\n    case_sensitive: bool = True\n    max_items: int = 100000\n    max_item_length: int = 10000\n    allow_empty_substring: bool = True\n    persist_path: Optional[str] = None\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringfilter/dto.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom .models import FilterConfig\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass FilterRequest:\n    \"\"\"Typed request container for filter operations.\"\"\"\n    items: List[str]\n    substring: str\n    config: Optional[FilterConfig] = None\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass FilterResponse:\n    \"\"\"Typed response container for filter operations.\"\"\"\n    result: List[str]\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringfilter/exceptions.py\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nclass FilterError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Domain-specific errors for the string filtering module.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str, code: Optional[int] = None) -> None:\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n        self.code = code\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringfilter/utils.py\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .exceptions import FilterError\nfrom .models import FilterConfig\n\nclass Validator:\n    \"\"\"Validates inputs against FilterConfig and business rules.\"\"\"\n\n    def validate_items(self, items: List[str], cfg: FilterConfig) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Checks type, length, and content of the items list.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(items, list):\n            raise FilterError(\"items must be a list of strings\", code=4001)\n        if len(items) > cfg.max_items:\n            raise FilterError(f\"too many items, max is {cfg.max_items}\", code=4002)\n        for item in items:\n            if not isinstance(item, str):\n                raise FilterError(\"each item must be a string\", code=4003)\n            self._validate_item_length(item, cfg)\n\n    def validate_substring(self, substring: str, cfg: FilterConfig) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Checks type and validity of the substring.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(substring, str):\n            raise FilterError(\"substring must be a string\", code=4004)\n        if substring == \"\" and not cfg.allow_empty_substring:\n            raise FilterError(\"empty substring not allowed by configuration\", code=4005)\n\n    def _validate_item_length(self, item: str, cfg: FilterConfig) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Helper to validate individual item length.\"\"\"\n        if len(item) > cfg.max_item_length:\n            raise FilterError(f\"item too long, max is {cfg.max_item_length}\", code=4006)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringfilter/string_repository.py\nimport json\nimport os\nimport tempfile\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .exceptions import FilterError\n\nclass StringRepository:\n    \"\"\"Provides abstract repository methods to read/write string lists, with file-backed implementation.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def load_from_file(path: str) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Reads a JSON array of strings from the specified file path.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                data = json.load(f)\n            if not isinstance(data, list) or not all(isinstance(i, str) for i in data):\n                raise FilterError(\"File content is not a valid JSON array of strings\", code=5001)\n            return data\n        except FileNotFoundError:\n            raise FilterError(f\"Input file not found: {path}\", code=5002)\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n            raise FilterError(f\"Invalid JSON in file {path}: {e}\", code=5003)\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise FilterError(f\"Failed to load from file {path}: {e}\", code=5004)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def save_to_file(path: str, items: List[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Writes a list of strings as a JSON array to the specified file path using atomic write.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            fd, temp_path = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=os.path.dirname(path), prefix=os.path.basename(path) + '.tmp-')\n            with os.fdopen(fd, 'w', encoding='utf-8') as tmp_f:\n                json.dump(items, tmp_f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n            os.replace(temp_path, path)\n        except Exception as e:\n            raise FilterError(f\"Failed to save to file {path}: {e}\", code=5005)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringfilter/filter_service.py\nfrom typing import List\nfrom .models import FilterConfig\nfrom .string_repository import StringRepository\nfrom .exceptions import FilterError\n\nclass FilterService:\n    \"\"\"Implements the core string filtering algorithm based on provided configuration.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, cfg: FilterConfig) -> None:\n        self._cfg = cfg\n\n    def filter_by_substring(self, items: List[str], substring: str) -> List[str]:\n        \"\"\"Filters a list of strings, returning only those containing the substring, respecting config.\"\"\"\n        if self._cfg.persist_path:\n            try:\n                StringRepository.save_to_file(self._cfg.persist_path, items)\n            except FilterError as e:\n                # Re-raise persistence errors from StringRepository\n                raise e\n            except Exception as e:\n                raise FilterError(f\"Failed to persist input: {e}\", code=6001)\n\n        if substring == \"\" and self._cfg.allow_empty_substring:\n            return list(items) # Return a copy of the original list\n\n        return [item for item in items if self._match(item, substring)]\n\n    def _match(self, item: str, substring: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Internal helper for the actual string matching logic.\"\"\"\n        if not self._cfg.case_sensitive:\n            return substring.lower() in item.lower()\n        return substring in item\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringfilter/filter_controller.py\nfrom .dto import FilterRequest, FilterResponse\nfrom .filter_service import FilterService\nfrom .utils import Validator\nfrom .models import FilterConfig # Needed to access config from request\n\nclass FilterController:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates request validation, service invocation, and response construction.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, service: FilterService, validator: Validator) -> None:\n        # The injected service here is a default/placeholder.\n        # For actual filtering, a service configured with the request's specific config will be used.\n        self._service = service\n        self._validator = validator\n\n    def handle_filter(self, request: FilterRequest) -> FilterResponse:\n        \"\"\"Handles a filter request, validates inputs, and returns the filtered results.\"\"\"\n        cfg = request.config if request.config else FilterConfig() # Use request config or default\n\n        self._validator.validate_items(request.items, cfg)\n        self._validator.validate_substring(request.substring, cfg)\n\n        # Create a FilterService instance with the specific configuration from the request\n        configured_service = FilterService(cfg)\n        result = configured_service.filter_by_substring(request.items, request.substring)\n\n        return FilterResponse(result)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringfilter/cli_adapter.py\nimport argparse\nimport sys\nimport json\nimport io\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom .dto import FilterRequest, FilterResponse\nfrom .models import FilterConfig\nfrom .filter_controller import FilterController\nfrom .filter_service import FilterService # For FilterController instantiation\nfrom .utils import Validator # For FilterController instantiation\nfrom .string_repository import StringRepository # For input file loading\nfrom .exceptions import FilterError\n\nclass CLIAdapter:\n    \"\"\"CLI entrypoint for string filtering, parsing arguments and presenting results.\"\"\"\n\n    def run(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parses CLI arguments, executes the filter operation, and prints results or errors.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            args = self._parse_args(argv)\n\n            items: List[str] = []\n            if args.input_file:\n                items = StringRepository.load_from_file(args.input_file)\n            elif not sys.stdin.isatty():\n                # Read newline-separated strings from stdin\n                items = [line.strip() for line in sys.stdin if line.strip()]\n\n            # Build FilterConfig from CLI args\n            cfg = FilterConfig(\n                case_sensitive=not args.case_insensitive,\n                persist_path=args.persist\n            )\n\n            # Instantiate controller with a default configured service and validator.\n            # The controller will then internally create a service with the request's config.\n            controller = FilterController(FilterService(cfg), Validator())\n            req = FilterRequest(items, args.substring, cfg)\n            resp = controller.handle_filter(req)\n\n            print(json.dumps({\"result\": resp.result}, indent=2))\n            return 0\n        except FilterError as e:\n            print(json.dumps({\"error\": e.message, \"code\": e.code}), file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Exit code for invalid input/validation errors\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(json.dumps({\"error\": f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\"}), file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # Exit code for general internal errors\n\n    def _parse_args(self, argv: List[str]) -> argparse.Namespace:\n        \"\"\"Parses command-line arguments using argparse.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n            description=\"Filter a list of strings by a substring.\",\n            formatter_class=argparse.ArgumentDefaultsHelpFormatter\n        )\n\n        subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest='command', required=True)\n\n        filter_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\n            'filter',\n            help='Filter strings based on a substring.'\n        )\n        filter_parser.add_argument(\n            '--substring',\n            '-s',\n            required=True,\n            help='The substring to filter by.'\n        )\n        filter_parser.add_argument(\n            '--input-file',\n            '-i',\n            type=str,\n            help='Path to a JSON file containing a list of strings. If not provided, reads from stdin.'\n        )\n        filter_parser.add_argument(\n            '--case-insensitive',\n            '-c',\n            action='store_true',\n            help='Perform case-insensitive matching.'\n        )\n        filter_parser.add_argument(\n            '--persist',\n            '-p',\n            type=str,\n            help='Optional path to a JSON file to persist the input list before filtering.'\n        )\n\n        return parser.parse_args(argv[1:])\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    \"\"\"Main entry point for the CLI.\"\"\"\n    cli_adapter = CLIAdapter()\n    sys.exit(cli_adapter.run(sys.argv))\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/stringfilter/api_adapter.py\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List\nimport os\nfrom .dto import FilterRequest, FilterResponse\nfrom .models import FilterConfig\nfrom .filter_controller import FilterController\nfrom .filter_service import FilterService\nfrom .utils import Validator\nfrom .exceptions import FilterError\n\n# Conditional import for Flask, as it's an optional dependency\ntry:\n    from flask import Flask, request, jsonify, Response\nexcept ImportError:\n    Flask = None\n    request = None\n    jsonify = None\n    Response = Any # Type hint for Flask.Response, fallback to Any\n\nclass APIAdapter:\n    \"\"\"Minimal HTTP adapter for POST /filter using Flask (optional dependency).\"\"\"\n\n    def create_app(self) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"Creates and configures a Flask application instance.\"\"\"\n        if Flask is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"Flask is not installed. Install with 'pip install stringfilter[http]' to use the API.\")\n\n        app = Flask(__name__)\n        app.add_url_rule('/filter', 'filter', self._post_filter, methods=['POST'])\n        return app\n\n    def _post_filter(self) -> Any:\n        \"\"\"Handles the POST /filter request, parses JSON, delegates to controller, and returns JSON response.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            data: Dict = request.get_json()\n            if not data:\n                raise FilterError(\"Request body must be valid JSON\", code=4000)\n\n            items = data.get('items')\n            substring = data.get('substring')\n            config_data = data.get('config')\n\n            if items is None or substring is None:\n                raise FilterError(\"Missing 'items' or 'substring' in request body\", code=4000)\n\n            cfg = FilterConfig(**config_data) if config_data else FilterConfig()\n            \n            # Instantiate controller with a default configured service and validator.\n            # The controller will then internally create a service with the request's config.\n            controller = FilterController(FilterService(cfg), Validator())\n            req = FilterRequest(items, substring, cfg)\n            resp: FilterResponse = controller.handle_filter(req)\n\n            return jsonify({\"result\": resp.result}), 200\n\n        except FilterError as e:\n            status_code = 422 if e.code and (e.code >= 4000 and e.code < 5000) else 400\n            return jsonify({\"error\": e.message, \"code\": e.code}), status_code\n        except Exception as e:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\"}), 500\n\n# This is for Flask's discovery mechanism (e.g., `flask run`)\nif Flask is not None:\n    app = APIAdapter().create_app()\n```"}
