{"task_id": "HumanEval/67", "solution": "```python\ndef fruit_distribution(s, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the number of mango fruits in a basket given a string with apple and orange counts\n    and the total number of fruits.\n    \"\"\"\n    apples = 0\n    oranges = 0\n\n    # Manually parse for apples count\n    s_lower = s.lower()\n    apple_keyword_index = s_lower.find(\"apple\")\n    if apple_keyword_index != -1:\n        # Search backward from the keyword to find the preceding number\n        current_index = apple_keyword_index - 1\n        num_chars = []\n        while current_index >= 0 and s[current_index].isdigit():\n            num_chars.insert(0, s[current_index])\n            current_index -= 1\n        if num_chars:\n            apples = int(\"\".join(num_chars))\n\n    # Manually parse for oranges count\n    orange_keyword_index = s_lower.find(\"orange\")\n    if orange_keyword_index != -1:\n        # Search backward from the keyword to find the preceding number\n        current_index = orange_keyword_index - 1\n        num_chars = []\n        while current_index >= 0 and s[current_index].isdigit():\n            num_chars.insert(0, s[current_index])\n            current_index -= 1\n        if num_chars:\n            oranges = int(\"\".join(num_chars))\n\n    # Calculate the number of mangoes\n    mangoes = n - apples - oranges\n    return mangoes\n```"}
