{"task_id": "HumanEval/76", "solution": "def is_simple_power(x, n):\n    \"\"\"Checks if x is an exact integer power of n (n**k == x for k >= 0).\n    Assumes x and n are positive integers based on problem examples.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return x == 1\n\n    # For n > 1, 1 is considered n**0.\n    if x == 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Repeatedly divide x by n while x is greater than 1 and divisible by n.\n    while x > 1 and x % n == 0:\n        x //= n\n\n    # If x has been reduced to 1, it means the original x was a power of n.\n    return x == 1"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/77", "solution": "def iscube(a):\n    # Determines if an integer 'a' is a perfect cube using binary search for its integer cube root.\n    # It calculates the integer cube root of |a| and then checks if its cube equals 'a'.\n    if a == 0:\n        k = 0\n    else:\n        sign = -1 if a < 0 else 1\n        m = abs(a)\n        lo, hi = 0, max(1, m)\n        k_abs = 0\n        while lo <= hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            cube = mid * mid * mid\n            if cube == m:\n                k_abs = mid\n                break\n            if cube < m:\n                k_abs = mid\n                lo = mid + 1\n            else:\n                hi = mid - 1\n        k = sign * k_abs\n    return k * k * k == a"}
