{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "def is_bored(S):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts \"boredoms\" in a text, where a boredom is a sentence starting with \"I\".\n    Sentences are delimited by '.', '?' or '!'.\n    \"\"\"\n    boredom_count = 0\n    \n    # Replace all sentence delimiters with a null character to facilitate splitting.\n    temp_s = S.replace('.', '\\x00').replace('?', '\\x00').replace('!', '\\x00')\n    \n    # Split the string into potential sentences using the null character.\n    sentence_candidates = temp_s.split('\\x00')\n    \n    for sentence_raw in sentence_candidates:\n        # Remove leading/trailing whitespace from each potential sentence.\n        sentence = sentence_raw.strip()\n        \n        # Skip if the sentence is empty after stripping whitespace.\n        if not sentence:\n            continue\n        \n        # Trim leading whitespace and specified left-side punctuation for first token check.\n        s_trimmed_leading = sentence.lstrip(' \\t\\n\"\\'([{')\n        \n        # If the sentence becomes empty after leading trim, skip it.\n        if not s_trimmed_leading:\n            continue\n            \n        # Extract the first token (word) from the trimmed sentence.\n        first_token = s_trimmed_leading.split(None, 1)[0]\n        \n        # Check if the first token is exactly \"I\" (case-sensitive).\n        if first_token == \"I\":\n            boredom_count += 1\n            \n    return boredom_count"}
