{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "def closest_integer(value):\n    '''\n    Returns the closest integer to a numeric string, rounding ties away from zero.\n    '''\n    f = float(value)\n\n    def _inline_floor(x):\n        # Computes the floor of a number, equivalent to math.floor.\n        i = int(x)\n        return i if i <= x else i - 1\n\n    def _inline_ceil(x):\n        # Computes the ceiling of a number, equivalent to math.ceil.\n        i = int(x)\n        return i if i >= x else i + 1\n\n    floor_val = _inline_floor(f)\n    ceil_val = _inline_ceil(f)\n\n    diff_floor = abs(f - floor_val)\n    diff_ceil = abs(ceil_val - f)\n\n    if diff_floor < diff_ceil:\n        return int(floor_val)\n    elif diff_ceil < diff_floor:\n        return int(ceil_val)\n    else:\n        # Tie-breaking: choose the integer with greater absolute value (away from zero).\n        return int(ceil_val if abs(ceil_val) > abs(floor_val) else floor_val)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\nfrom decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP, ROUND_CEILING, ROUND_FLOOR, Context, localcontext\n\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a numeric string to the closest integer, rounding ties away from zero.\n    Accepts standard numeric formats including decimals and exponents.\n    \"\"\"\n    DECIMAL_CONTEXT = Context(prec=28) # Define Decimal context with specified precision.\n\n    with localcontext(DECIMAL_CONTEXT):\n        # Parse the input string into a Decimal.\n        # The 'strip()' method handles leading/trailing whitespace.\n        d = Decimal(value.strip())\n\n        # Determine if the number is exactly halfway between two integers (e.g., 14.5, -14.5).\n        # We calculate the positive fractional part by subtracting the floor of d from d.\n        # d.to_integral_value(rounding=ROUND_FLOOR) computes floor(d).\n        fractional_part = d - d.to_integral_value(rounding=ROUND_FLOOR)\n        is_halfway = (fractional_part == Decimal('0.5'))\n\n        if is_halfway:\n            # Apply \"round away from zero\" rule for ties.\n            if d >= 0:\n                # For positive halves (e.g., 14.5), round up (towards positive infinity).\n                rounded_decimal = d.quantize(Decimal('1'), rounding=ROUND_CEILING)\n            else:\n                # For negative halves (e.g., -14.5), round down (towards negative infinity).\n                rounded_decimal = d.quantize(Decimal('1'), rounding=ROUND_FLOOR)\n        else:\n            # If not a tie, round to the nearest integer.\n            # ROUND_HALF_UP rounds to nearest, with halves going towards positive infinity.\n            # This mode correctly rounds non-ties to the nearest integer for both positive and negative numbers.\n            rounded_decimal = d.quantize(Decimal('1'), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)\n\n        # Convert the final Decimal result to an integer.\n        return int(rounded_decimal)\n```"}
