{"task_id": "HumanEval/108", "solution": "```python\ndef count_nums(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts elements in an array where the sum of signed digits is positive.\n    Negative numbers have their most significant digit negated for the sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_count = 0\n    for num in arr:\n        is_negative = num < 0\n        abs_num_str = str(abs(num))\n        \n        current_digit_sum = 0\n        \n        if is_negative:\n            # For negative numbers, the first digit is negative, others positive.\n            current_digit_sum -= int(abs_num_str[0])\n            for digit_char in abs_num_str[1:]:\n                current_digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n        else:\n            # For non-negative numbers, all digits are positive.\n            for digit_char in abs_num_str:\n                current_digit_sum += int(digit_char)\n        \n        if current_digit_sum > 0:\n            total_count += 1\n            \n    return total_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/108", "solution": "```python\ndef count_nums(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts elements in an array where the signed-digit sum is > 0.\n    Negative numbers have the sign on the most significant digit.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for n in arr:\n        # Calculate signed digits for number n\n        if n == 0:\n            signed_digits = [0]\n        else:\n            is_negative = n < 0\n            abs_n_str = str(abs(n))\n            \n            digits = []\n            for i, digit_char in enumerate(abs_n_str):\n                digit = int(digit_char)\n                if i == 0 and is_negative:\n                    digits.append(-digit)\n                else:\n                    digits.append(digit)\n            signed_digits = digits\n\n        # Sum the signed digits\n        current_sum = sum(signed_digits)\n\n        # Increment count if the sum is greater than 0\n        if current_sum > 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/109", "solution": "```python\ndef move_one_ball(arr):\n    \"\"\"We have an array 'arr' of N integers arr[1], arr[2], ..., arr[N].\n    The function checks if the array can be sorted into non-decreasing order by performing right shift operations.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    drops = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        nxt = (i + 1) % n\n        if arr[i] > arr[nxt]:\n            drops += 1\n            if drops > 1:\n                return False\n    return True\n```"}
