{"task_id": "HumanEval/111", "solution": "```python\ndef histogram(test):\n    \"\"\"Given a string of space-separated lowercase letters, return a dictionary\n    of the letter(s) with the highest repetition count.\n    If multiple letters share the same highest count, include all of them.\n    \"\"\"\n    tokens = test.strip().split()\n    counts = {}\n\n    for token in tokens:\n        # Only count tokens that are single lowercase ASCII letters.\n        if len(token) == 1 and 'a' <= token <= 'z':\n            counts[token] = counts.get(token, 0) + 1\n\n    if not counts:\n        return {}\n\n    max_count = 0\n    for count in counts.values():\n        if count > max_count:\n            max_count = count\n\n    result = {}\n    for letter, count in counts.items():\n        if count == max_count:\n            result[letter] = count\n            \n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/111", "solution": "from typing import Dict\n\ndef histogram(test: str) -> Dict[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"Given a string of space-separated lowercase letters, compute the highest repetition count.\n    Return a dictionary of all letters with this maximum count.\n    \"\"\"\n    tokens = [t for t in test.split(' ') if t != '']\n\n    if not tokens:\n        return {}\n\n    counts = {}\n    for token in tokens:\n        counts[token] = counts.get(token, 0) + 1\n\n    max_count = 0\n    if counts:\n        max_count = max(counts.values())\n\n    result = {letter: count for letter, count in counts.items() if count == max_count}\n    return result"}
