{"task_id": "HumanEval/114", "solution": "```python\ndef minSubArraySum(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of integers nums, find the minimum sum of any non-empty sub-array.\n    This implementation uses a modified Kadane's algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_ending_here = nums[0]\n    min_so_far = nums[0]\n\n    for num in nums[1:]:\n        min_ending_here = min(num, min_ending_here + num)\n        min_so_far = min(min_so_far, min_ending_here)\n\n    return min_so_far\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/113", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_count(lst):\n    \"\"\"Given a list of strings of digits, returns formatted strings describing odd digit counts.\n    Every 'i' in the template is replaced by the count of odd digits for that string.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    template = \"the number of odd elements in the string i of the input.\"\n\n    for s in lst:\n        odd_digit_count = 0\n        for char_digit in s:\n            # Convert char to int and check if it's odd\n            if int(char_digit) % 2 == 1:\n                odd_digit_count += 1\n\n        repl_str = str(odd_digit_count)\n        # Build the formatted string by replacing each 'i' in the template\n        formatted_template = \"\".join([repl_str if char_in_template == 'i' else char_in_template for char_in_template in template])\n        results.append(formatted_template)\n\n    return results\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/114", "solution": "```python\ndef minSubArraySum(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of integers nums, find the minimum sum of any non-empty sub-array.\n    This implementation uses a modified Kadane's algorithm to track the minimum sum and its indices.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_ending_here = nums[0]\n    min_so_far = nums[0]\n    s = 0  # Start index of the current subarray ending at 'i'\n    start = 0  # Start index of the overall minimum subarray\n    end = 0  # End index of the overall minimum subarray\n\n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        # Determine if extending the current subarray or starting a new one yields a smaller sum ending at 'i'.\n        if min_ending_here + nums[i] > nums[i]:\n            min_ending_here = nums[i]\n            s = i\n        else:\n            min_ending_here += nums[i]\n\n        # Update the overall minimum sum found so far, applying tie-breaking rules.\n        if min_ending_here < min_so_far:\n            min_so_far = min_ending_here\n            start = s\n            end = i\n        elif min_ending_here == min_so_far:\n            # Tie-breaker: prefer earliest start index.\n            if s < start:\n                start = s\n                end = i\n            # Tie-breaker: if same start index, prefer shorter length.\n            elif s == start and (i - s) < (end - start):\n                end = i\n                \n    return min_so_far\n```"}
