{"task_id": "HumanEval/153", "solution": "def Strongest_Extension(class_name, extensions):\n    \"\"\"Computes the strongest extension based on CAP - SM metric.\n    Tie-breaking: first occurrence in list wins.\"\"\"\n    strongest_extension_name = \"\"\n    max_strength = -float('inf')\n\n    for extension_name in extensions:\n        cap_count = 0\n        sm_count = 0\n        for char in extension_name:\n            if char.isupper():\n                cap_count += 1\n            elif char.islower():\n                sm_count += 1\n        current_strength = cap_count - sm_count\n\n        # Select extension with maximum strength; tie-breaker: earliest list order\n        if current_strength > max_strength:\n            max_strength = current_strength\n            strongest_extension_name = extension_name\n\n    return f\"{class_name}.{strongest_extension_name}\""}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/154", "solution": "def cycpattern_check(a , b):\n    \"\"\"Checks if the second word or any of its cyclic rotations is a substring in the first word.\n    Returns True if a match is found, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    n = len(b)\n    if n == 0:\n        return False  # Per business rule: empty target returns False\n\n    # Generate unique cyclic rotations of b\n    unique_rotations = []\n    seen_rotations = set()\n    for i in range(n):\n        rotation = b[i:] + b[:i]\n        if rotation not in seen_rotations:\n            unique_rotations.append(rotation)\n            seen_rotations.add(rotation)\n    \n    # Check if any unique rotation is a substring of a\n    for rotation in unique_rotations:\n        if rotation in a:\n            return True\n            \n    return False"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/155", "solution": "def even_odd_count(num):\n    \"\"\"Given an integer, return a tuple with the number of even and odd digits.\n    The sign of the input integer is ignored for counting.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_num = str(abs(num))\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n    for digit_char in s_num:\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        if digit % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n    return (even_count, odd_count)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/154", "solution": "```python\ndef cycpattern_check(a , b):\n    \"\"\"You are given 2 words. You need to return True if the second word or any of its rotations is a substring in the first word.\n    The check is case-sensitive.\n    \"\"\"\n    len_b = len(b)\n    if len_b == 0 or len_b > len(a):\n        return False\n\n    # Concatenate 'b' with itself to form a string that contains all its cyclic rotations as substrings.\n    doubled_b = b + b\n\n    # Check if any rotation of 'b' (which is a substring of 'doubled_b' of length len_b) exists in 'a'.\n    for i in range(len_b):\n        rotation = doubled_b[i : i + len_b]\n        if rotation in a:\n            return True\n\n    return False\n```"}
